🔍 STEP 2: Verify Terraform Resources Exist

Run:

terraform state list

You should see:

VPC
Subnets
NAT
Route tables
✍️ STEP 3: Add Kubernetes Tags to Subnets

This is CRITICAL.

Without these tags:

Load Balancers fail
EKS networking breaks
✅ Public Subnet Tags

Inside BOTH public subnet blocks:

tags = {
  Name = "public-subnet-1"

  "kubernetes.io/role/elb" = "1"
  "kubernetes.io/cluster/ecommerce-cluster" = "shared"
}

Second public subnet:

tags = {
  Name = "public-subnet-2"

  "kubernetes.io/role/elb" = "1"
  "kubernetes.io/cluster/ecommerce-cluster" = "shared"
}
✅ Private Subnet Tags
tags = {
  Name = "private-subnet-1"

  "kubernetes.io/role/internal-elb" = "1"
  "kubernetes.io/cluster/ecommerce-cluster" = "shared"
}

Second private subnet:

tags = {
  Name = "private-subnet-2"

  "kubernetes.io/role/internal-elb" = "1"
  "kubernetes.io/cluster/ecommerce-cluster" = "shared"
}
🧠 Why These Tags Matter
Tag	Purpose
kubernetes.io/role/elb	Public ALB
kubernetes.io/role/internal-elb	Internal Load Balancer
kubernetes.io/cluster/...	EKS discovers subnets
▶️ STEP 4: Apply Terraform Changes

Run:

terraform apply

Type:

yes
🔍 STEP 5: Get Subnet IDs

Go to:

AWS Console
→ VPC
→ Subnets

Copy:

Public subnet IDs

Example:

subnet-11111
subnet-22222
Private subnet IDs

Example:

subnet-33333
subnet-44444
🧠 IMPORTANT

Make sure:

Public subnets = map public IP enabled
Private subnets = no public IP
🚀 STEP 6: Create EKS Cluster in Existing VPC

Create EKS Using YOUR VPC:

eksctl create cluster \
--name Ecommerce-cluster \
--region ap-southeast-2 \
--vpc-private-subnets subnet-0b7021a2024a48289,subnet-0887ef050db0f9e28 \
--vpc-public-subnets subnet-0f2ce81535f673121,subnet-07073ed0583842053 \
--nodegroup-name workers \
--node-type t3.medium \
--nodes 2 \
--managed


🧠 Deep Explanation of This Command
--vpc-private-subnets

Worker nodes go here.

Why?

Secure
No public exposure
Industry best practice
--vpc-public-subnets

ALB will use these later.

Why?

Internet users need app access
--managed

AWS manages:

Node health
Updates
Scaling integrations
⏳ STEP 7: Wait Patiently

Cluster creation takes:

15–25 minutes

Do NOT close terminal.

