🔍 STEP 1: Verify Cluster Connectivity

Run:

kubectl get nodes

Expected:

STATUS = Ready
🔍 STEP 2: Create Namespace

Namespaces logically separate applications.

Run:

kubectl create namespace ecommerce

Verify:

kubectl get namespaces
🧠 Why Namespace?

Real companies separate:

dev
qa
prod

using namespaces.

📁 STEP 3: Create Kubernetes Folder Structure

Inside project root:

mkdir -p k8s/nginx
cd k8s/nginx
✍️ STEP 4: Create Deployment YAML

Create file:

touch deployment.yaml

Open in VS Code.

Paste:

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: nginx-deployment
  namespace: ecommerce

spec:
  replicas: 2

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx

    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:latest

        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
🧠 Deep Understanding
replicas: 2

Creates:

2 Pods

Why?

High availability
Load distribution
image: nginx:latest

Pulls Docker image from:
Docker Hub

containerPort: 80

Container listens on port 80.

▶️ STEP 5: Deploy Application

Run:

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
🔍 STEP 6: Verify Deployment

Run:

kubectl get deployments -n ecommerce

Expected:

READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE
2/2
🔍 STEP 7: Verify Pods

Run:

kubectl get pods -n ecommerce

Expected:

2 Running pods
🧠 What Happened Internally?

Kubernetes:

Deployment
   ↓
ReplicaSet
   ↓
Pods
   ↓
Containers
🔥 STEP 8: Expose Application

Now create Service.

Create file:

touch service.yaml

Paste:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service

metadata:
  name: nginx-service
  namespace: ecommerce

spec:
  selector:
    app: nginx

  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80
      targetPort: 80

  type: LoadBalancer
🧠 Why Service?

Pods are temporary.

Service gives:

Stable networking
Load balancing
Single access point
🧠 Why LoadBalancer?

Because on AWS:

Service Type LoadBalancer
        ↓
Creates AWS ELB automatically

This is huge interview knowledge.

▶️ STEP 9: Apply Service

Run:

kubectl apply -f service.yaml
🔍 STEP 10: Verify Service

Run:

kubectl get svc -n ecommerce

Initially:

EXTERNAL-IP = pending

Wait 2–5 mins.

Then:

EXTERNAL-IP = <AWS LoadBalancer DNS>
🌐 STEP 11: Access Application

Copy EXTERNAL-IP.

Open in browser:

http://<external-ip>

You should see:

Welcome to nginx!
